STATUS: RULED 2026-10-24 — surface settled, test respelled.

## The ruling

Compiler annotations on TYPE positions LIVE, as a dedicated AST field
(`type_annotations`), distinct from `<>` phantoms:

- `Type[x]` — compiler annotation (opaque string, any content; comma list
  for several). Inert metadata read by transforms.
- `Type<x>` — phantom state, unchanged.
- `Type<x>[x]` — stacks: phantom inner on the type name, annotation
  outermost.

The invocation-side echo is DEAD: a call site may not repeat the tag. The
`<type>"path"` typed file source and `<Type>{` typed source block were
removed; `@"path"` and a bare `{` are the only file/block source closures.
The kind is declared once — `source: Source[text]` — and reaches the proc
through the existing `source.phantom_type` channel.

## What this test pins

`source: Source[text]` parses (annotation extracted, `type` stays "Source")
and `~render.file @"hello.txt"` reads the file at comptime, delivering the
declared tag. Resolves NEEDS_RULING together with 310_040; sibling 210_024
stays parked on the unrelated continuation-position emitter/transform gaps.
